From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:03:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] QueueInstance::getAudio: move on from a source that gives no
 audio

A looping sound in a queue returns no frames at its end but never ends, as
queued sources are not rewound, so the read loop never exited and the mix
hung. A source that gives no audio is now treated as finished.
---
 src/core/soloud_queue.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud_queue.cpp b/src/core/soloud_queue.cpp
index 98c0d91..bce528a 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud_queue.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud_queue.cpp
@@ -45,7 +45,9 @@ namespace SoLoud
 			int readcount = mParent->mSource[mParent->mReadIndex]->getAudio(aBuffer + copyofs, copycount, aBufferSize);
 			copyofs += readcount;
 			copycount -= readcount;
-			if (mParent->mSource[mParent->mReadIndex]->hasEnded())
+			// A source that gives no audio without ending (a looping sound at its
+			// end: nothing rewinds queued sources) would never be left.
+			if (readcount == 0 || mParent->mSource[mParent->mReadIndex]->hasEnded())
 			{
 				delete mParent->mSource[mParent->mReadIndex];
 				mParent->mSource[mParent->mReadIndex] = 0;
